{% comment %}
  Page transition overlay — two-layer system:

    1. Departing page: intercept same-origin link clicks.
       Backdrop blur builds immediately → overlay slides up from bottom
       while blur is still in progress → navigate.

    2. Arriving page: only animates when arriving from an internal
       navigation (sessionStorage flag).  On first load / reload the
       overlay is hidden instantly.

  Both layers start with the `hidden` attribute so the UA stylesheet's
  `[hidden] { display: none }` hides them before any CSS loads — no
  FOUC, no stuck overlay if the author stylesheet is late.
{% endcomment %}

<div
  id="PageTransitionBlur"
  class="page-transition-blur"
  hidden
  aria-hidden="true"
></div>

<div
  id="PageTransitionOverlay"
  class="page-transition-overlay"
  style="background-color: var(--color-background)"
  hidden
  aria-hidden="true"
></div>

<script defer src="{{ 'page-transition.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
